 "how": "Facts copied from the documents in this folder. Each was matched by script to the words on the page cited. 'must' = on the site, next to it, or within 5 km; 'should' = further out or position not stated; 'none_expected' = the document says there are none within distance_km.",
 "distance_basis": "As stated in the document: from the site boundary or from the nearest turbine (see each note).",
 "notes": [
  "Replaces the earlier outcome built from online reading: the folder now holds the right documents, the Scottish Ministers' decision letter (with the Reporter's public inquiry report bound in) and Kirkton's own Non-Technical Summary (November 2022).",
  "Polygon: 423 ha in four parts (main site plus the turning-area exclaves north of the A836). The inquiry report gives about 419 ha. It matches.",
  "Pages are PDF pages, not the printed numbers.",
  "Distances are as stated: some from the site boundary, some from the nearest turbine (see each note).",
  "East Halladale Flows WLA: 1.29 km from the site in the decision letter, about 2 km from the nearest turbine in the summary.",
  "The SAC: the summary says it and West Halladale SSSI reach slightly into the boundary; the decision letter says the site is adjacent. Kept as on the site.",
  "Hindsight: the Flow Country was inscribed in July 2024 (p3; p22 says June), after the 2022 application. The application went in a couple of months before the candidate nomination.",
  "The DPEA case reference is WIN-270-21. The letter gives no ECU number, so the portal reference in the site list (ECU00003226) is still unconfirmed."
